<title>UK: Capital says offer fails to see potential.</title>
<headline>Capital says offer fails to see potential.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Casino operator Capital Corp Plc, said a hostile bid from London Clubs International Plc fails to take account of its potential.</p>
<p>&quot;As we have said already this offer takes no account of our potential now that we have two fully operational high roller clubs,&quot; said chief executive Alan Hearn in a statement.</p>
<p>London Club's all paper offer launched on February 17, values Capital at about 181 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;It also fails to reflect the value of the Crockfords name and our unique position in London, where we have grown our market share in each of the last five years,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
